WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.101
-Thank you very much, everybody!

00:00:02.101 --> 00:00:04.036
Hello!
Wow.

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.571
That feels great.

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:09.008
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.778
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.747
I'd like to start by wishing
everyone a very happy new year.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.750
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.752
Yep. Thankfully,
it is a new year,

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.921
and, boy,
aren't things better now?

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:24.857
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.857 --> 00:00:26.592
Well, guys,
everybody is talking about this.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:28.060
Over the weekend,
President Trump

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.829
called Georgia
Secretary of State,

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.998
Brad Raffensperger,
about the election

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:35.635
and might have gotten himself
into some major legal trouble.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:39.472
"Let's hear what
crime it was this time!"

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.717
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.686
That's right.
Trump asked him to somehow

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.655
find enough votes
to flip Georgia

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.391
so that he would win the state
by one vote.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.027
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.662
One vote.
Trump was like,

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.998
"'Cause if we're gonna do this,
we can't make it obvious."

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.800
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.102
Apparently, every January,
Trump's New Year's resolution

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:11.838
is to find a new way
to get impeached.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.539
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:16.242
Trump's call lasted for an hour,
by the way.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.943
An hour.
It was like one of his calls

00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:20.079
to "Fox &amp; Friends,"
except he actually cared

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:21.614
what the other person
had to say on this one.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.416
[ Laughter ]
What a waste.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.450
Trump could've spent that hour

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.085
not helping roll out
the vaccine.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.455
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.855
As if the story
isn't crazy enough,

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:34.160
Trump had tried calling him
18 times since the election.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.861
Yeah.
I think we're one call away

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:37.730
from Trump saying,
"I'm on your front porch.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.298
I can see you're home.
Pick up.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:41.367
I can see you're screening
the call, you're making eggs.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:42.435
Hello.
I'm right here."

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.703
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:45.538
18 times!

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:47.540
Apparently, Raffensperger
was thinking about

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.443
putting the phone on vibrate
and turning it into a massager.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:52.745
[ Cellphone vibrating ]

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.147
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:57.216
[ Cellphone vibrating ]

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.519
That cost us $100,000
for that sound.

00:01:59.519 --> 00:02:01.254
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.355
You know you've --
[ Cellphone vibrating ]

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:05.357
No, thank you.
$150,000.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:07.359
You know you've lost power
when someone gets a call

00:02:07.359 --> 00:02:10.163
from the president
and presses ignore 18 times.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.331
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.566
When Trump calls,
people actually move to the room

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.267
in the house
where the connection is spotty.

00:02:15.267 --> 00:02:16.869
It's like, "Honey,
I'll be in the crawl space.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.138
Trump's trying to call me."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:21.007
Hey, are you that talk-show --
that game-show host?

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:23.877
"That's right."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:28.314
Carl Bernstein said Trump's call
was far worse than Watergate.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.783
Doesn't mean much to Trump.
He thinks Watergate is about

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.685
toilets not flushing
hard enough.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.353
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:37.423
"Sometimes you have to flush it
two, three times."

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:40.426
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:43.462
Trump tried everything to
persuade the Secretary of State,

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:44.864
but he wouldn't budge.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.833
Later, Trump told Raffensperger,

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.968
"Come on. You were such
a nice guy on 'Cheers.'

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.871
What happened to you?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.307
"Yeah, that's what you call
voter fraud there, Sammy."

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:56.175
[ Laughter ]
Thank you very much.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:57.509
Thank you very much.
-Nice, nice.

00:02:57.509 --> 00:02:59.078
-I break it out
every now and then. Thank you.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:03.950
Another combination --
pull it out, put it back in.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.486
"Yeah, that's what you call
voter fraud there, Sammy."

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.088
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.923
Yep, Trump's call
just kept going.

00:03:10.923 --> 00:03:12.625
Listen to what else
he had to say.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:23.095
-Interesting, right?
[ Applause ]

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.164
"Pw-e-e-ease?"

00:04:25.164 --> 00:04:26.799
And a lot of people
are talking about this.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:29.969
On Wednesday, Congress is set
to certify Joe Biden's victory,

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:31.503
but 12 Republican Senators

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:33.939
have pledged
to challenge the results.

00:04:33.939 --> 00:04:36.408
Can we see
the 12 Republican senators?

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:38.277
It looks like the chart
of different haircuts

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:40.179
you get at
a Supercuts in Idaho.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.214
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.016
They are the head shots
if you were casting a movie

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.919
about an evil lawyer
who swindles an orphanage.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:50.056
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.757
That's the cast of "Oceans 12"

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:53.693
if they were robbing
an L.L.Bean.

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.127
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:57.162
Meanwhile, all eyes will be
on Georgia tomorrow

00:04:57.162 --> 00:04:59.031
for the state's
two runoff races,

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.534
which will determine
the Senate majority.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.069
Another Election Night?

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:06.805
All right!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:09.475
Yep, the election is tomorrow,
which means we should have

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:13.713
the results by approximately
Cinco de Mayo.

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.114
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.049
That's right, it's a big night.
In fact, Brian Williams

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:19.786
is already doing
his voice exercises.

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:23.956
"It is too close to call.
It is too close to call.

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:27.860
It is too close to call."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:31.364
"Are you the game-show host?"
"You betcha, yeah!"

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:33.666
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.301
Yep.
Everyone's focused on Georgia's

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.569
Senate election, and now
several members of Congress

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.338
are speaking out
about the runoffs.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:41.907
For example,
Republican Congressman Bob Good

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:43.910
said if the Republicans
win both races,

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.013
then I will feel very,
well, my last name."

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.181
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:50.750
Then Democratic Congresswoman
Susan Wild said,

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.218
"If the Republicans
win both races,

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:54.921
that'd be absolutely,
well, my last name."

00:05:54.921 --> 00:05:56.455
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:59.124
Then Republican Andy Barr said,
"If the Democrats pull this off

00:05:59.124 --> 00:06:01.861
I'm gonna spend every night
at the, well, my last name."

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:02.995
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:05.030
Then, Congresswoman
Virginia Foxx said,

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:06.732
"I might be a Republican,
but I can't deny

00:06:06.732 --> 00:06:09.602
that Jon Ossoff is a total,
well, my last name."

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:10.770
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:13.539
Then Republican Congressman
French Hill said,

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.708
"If the Democrats beat us,
I'm gonna pack my bags

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.177
and move to,
well, my full name."

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:19.478
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:22.181
And finally, Missouri Senator
Roy Blunt said,

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:24.150
"Whoever wins,
I'mma order some Papa John's

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:26.184
and roll a big giant spliff."

00:06:26.184 --> 00:06:31.958
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:34.827
Some sports news.
Guys, the NFL regular season

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:36.662
is over,
and for the first time

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:40.565
since 2002 the Cleveland Browns
are going to the playoffs.

00:06:40.565 --> 00:06:44.437
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:46.972
Even Georgia Secretary of State
was like, "That can't be right.

00:06:46.972 --> 00:06:49.141
Count the wins again."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:50.709
When they heard that
they made the playoffs,

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:53.546
the Browns were like, "There's
more games after the season?"

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:56.315
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.315 --> 00:07:00.353
"Do they do that every year?"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:01.954
"Wow."

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.790
Yeah, the Browns
are going to the playoffs.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.691
Fans are like, "Thanks.
The one year

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:08.260
we can't be there in person.
You gotta be kidding me."

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.862
Right now, the people
of Cleveland are thinking,

00:07:09.862 --> 00:07:12.464
"Even when we win, we lose."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:14.733
Some business news.
I saw that Pizza Hut

00:07:14.733 --> 00:07:18.304
is celebrating 25 years
of its famous stuffed crust

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.506
by giving away
a stuffed crust pizza

00:07:20.506 --> 00:07:23.476
without the actual pizza.
Take a look at this.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:25.978
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:28.347
It's great if you want a pizza
that more closely resembles

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:30.849
an unrolled condom.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.849 --> 00:07:33.685
-Ha!
[ Cymbals crash ]

00:07:33.685 --> 00:07:40.025
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:40.025 --> 00:07:41.526
-Seriously,
what could be more exciting

00:07:41.526 --> 00:07:43.896
than sinking your teeth
into a soggy cheese tire?

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.431
[ Laughter ]
Here's how they do it.

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:47.566
First, they make the pizza,
then the delivery guy

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:49.902
eats it from the inside out
before handing it to you.

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:52.104
Takes practice,
but you can do it.

00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:53.438
Some entertainment news.

00:07:53.438 --> 00:07:57.476
I saw that a Rubik's cube movie
is now in the works.

00:07:57.476 --> 00:08:01.113
I don't know about you,
I'm not streaming that movie.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.883
A Rubik's cube is meant to be
enjoyed on the big screen.

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:07.853
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.853 --> 00:08:09.889
I'm sure it'll be great, though.
It's basically "Spider-Man"

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:12.425
if Peter Parker
never got bit by a spider.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:15.827
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.827 --> 00:08:18.197
And, finally, this is strange.
I saw that a seemingly

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:23.435
normal house for sale in Vermont
has an entire jail inside.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:26.038
Man, as a parent, you could
really put a kid in a time-out.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.007
I mean, wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:30.610
The listing agent was like,
"It comes with hardwood floors,

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:32.711
a large backyard, and Carl,

00:08:32.711 --> 00:08:34.547
who's serving 10 to 15
for armed robbery.

00:08:34.547 --> 00:08:37.616
[ Laughter ]
"I'm hungry."

00:08:37.616 --> 00:08:39.985
The previous owner decided
to sell because the overhead

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:41.420
was a little high,
and he was tired

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.722
of getting shivved
every morning.

